WEBVTT

00:10.750 --> 00:12.750
<b>Farming Life in Another World</b>

00:12.540 --> 00:20.130
When you open your eyes and see
that pure white light, the story begins

00:20.130 --> 00:26.880
Stepping forth into a new world,
what kind of flowers will we make bloom?

00:27.080 --> 00:34.460
Even if it's cloudy,
even if we get dirty from a puddle

00:34.460 --> 00:37.290
We continue on

00:37.290 --> 00:44.040
There's a future we can't imagine
waiting for us, I'm sure of it

00:44.330 --> 00:47.920
Meeting, meeting, and connecting

00:47.920 --> 00:51.210
If you smile,
everyone around you will smile too

00:51.210 --> 00:55.250
Let's plant a small seed and nurture it

00:55.250 --> 00:59.330
One day it'll become a large flower

00:59.330 --> 01:02.880
Turn regrets and failures into fuel

01:02.880 --> 01:06.170
So that you're overflowing with colorful happiness

01:06.170 --> 01:10.380
We'll join hands and share

01:10.380 --> 01:16.210
Spread across the world, Flower Ring

01:34.920 --> 01:37.830
Today we're all enjoying
another peaceful morning.

01:39.000 --> 01:42.000
The Great Tree Village
has become quite lively lately.

01:44.790 --> 01:45.670
One, two...

01:45.670 --> 01:48.420
My day starts once the sun has
completely risen each morning.

01:48.420 --> 01:50.130
That's when I wake up.

01:52.210 --> 01:53.460
Good morning.

01:53.880 --> 01:55.500
Hey, good morning.

01:56.000 --> 01:57.750
Are you feeling alright?

01:57.750 --> 02:00.920
Jeez, you ask me that
every time you see me.

02:00.920 --> 02:02.630
Oh, do I?

02:02.960 --> 02:05.040
But I'm sure things are tough for you.

02:05.040 --> 02:07.540
Once we found out that
Lu was pregnant,

02:07.540 --> 02:10.540
the entire village went into a joyous uproar.

02:10.790 --> 02:13.920
So that's why I haven't been
able to transform.

02:14.040 --> 02:16.250
I-is that how it works?

02:16.250 --> 02:18.330
She was the calmest out of everyone.

02:18.670 --> 02:21.420
You don't need to worry so much.

02:21.420 --> 02:23.380
I'm sure everything will be fine.

02:24.710 --> 02:25.710
Is that right?

02:26.170 --> 02:27.170
It is.

02:27.460 --> 02:30.380
I'm going to go check on
the medicinal herb garden.

02:30.380 --> 02:32.080
Okay. Are you alright going by yourself?

02:32.080 --> 02:33.130
You're doing it again.

02:33.130 --> 02:34.540
Ah, sorry.

02:36.080 --> 02:37.960
Now back to my morning schedule.

02:38.460 --> 02:40.080
According to Anne and the maids,

02:40.080 --> 02:43.080
it's my job to keep an eye
on things around the house.

02:43.080 --> 02:44.460
Good morning.

02:44.830 --> 02:46.460
Hey. Morning.

02:46.460 --> 02:50.210
By the way, there's a reason I don't
wake up too early in the morning.

02:51.380 --> 02:56.080
Anne and the other maids all insist on
waking up earlier than I do.

02:56.580 --> 02:58.790
I sleep later for their sakes.

02:58.790 --> 03:01.080
I'm definitely not being lazy.

03:01.540 --> 03:03.130
When I see her in the morning,

03:03.130 --> 03:05.330
she lets me know if she has
anything to report.

03:05.330 --> 03:08.460
Last night the wine slime
snuck into the food storage area

03:08.460 --> 03:10.380
and drank and entire barrel of wine.

03:10.380 --> 03:13.380
Was that the barrel that we left out
to keep the wine slime away from the rest?

03:13.380 --> 03:16.380
Yes. I'm not sure if we should
celebrate our plan working,

03:16.380 --> 03:19.880
or if we should be lamenting the fact
that we let it sneak in at all.

03:20.130 --> 03:22.630
Let's just say it went according to plan.

03:22.960 --> 03:25.710
Once I've made my rounds around the house,
it's time for breakfast.

03:25.710 --> 03:28.130
We can't fit everyone into
the dining hall at once,

03:28.130 --> 03:30.380
so we split breakfast up
into three groups.

03:30.380 --> 03:32.250
For today's main breakfast menu,

03:32.250 --> 03:35.460
we have a soup of daikon radish,
spinach, and cabbage.

03:35.460 --> 03:38.130
We also have smoked killer rabbit
that we've seared to finish.

03:38.130 --> 03:39.500
Thank you.

03:39.750 --> 03:40.960
It looks great.

03:41.880 --> 03:42.290
One microorganism, two microorganisms...

03:42.290 --> 03:43.380
Flora?
One microorganism, two microorganisms...<b></b>

03:43.380 --> 03:44.130
One microorganism, two microorganisms...

03:44.130 --> 03:46.130
Have you not been sleeping?
One microorganism, two microorganisms...<b></b>

03:46.130 --> 03:48.630
I haven't been making any progress
on the miso production.

03:48.630 --> 03:54.380
<b>Taste-testing miso</b>

03:48.880 --> 03:50.920
I guess this is about 20% of the way there...

03:51.920 --> 03:54.380
It's because you say stuff like that.

03:55.170 --> 03:57.000
I'm sure I just need more of this stuff.

03:57.000 --> 03:59.420
I apologize, and I implore you
to get some sleep.

04:00.210 --> 04:02.170
The second breakfast group is the maids.

04:02.170 --> 04:03.880
Finally, the third group

04:03.880 --> 04:06.670
is whoever didn't make it in time
for the first or second groups.

04:07.000 --> 04:11.830
Sometimes Hakuren doesn't even
make it in time for the third group.

04:12.830 --> 04:14.710
Mayor, I'm here to make a report.

04:14.710 --> 04:16.080
Did something happen?

04:16.380 --> 04:20.540
Yesterday, a group of three killer rabbits
attempted to infiltrate the village.

04:20.540 --> 04:22.580
However, Kuro and the dogs
were able to eliminate them.

04:22.960 --> 04:25.670
I see.
Those rabbits never learn their lesson.

04:25.670 --> 04:27.790
Well, we are able to use them as food,

04:27.790 --> 04:31.580
so we should be thankful that
they act the way they do.

04:31.580 --> 04:32.710
Good point.

04:33.170 --> 04:36.210
You know, even though
Granmaria and the other angels

04:36.210 --> 04:38.040
always seem so composed and proper,

04:38.040 --> 04:41.170
they all enter lazy mode when they're
off duty and on their own time.

04:41.920 --> 04:43.630
They can't really do any chores.

04:43.630 --> 04:45.500
Anne and the maids prepare their food,

04:45.500 --> 04:48.000
while they rely on Daga
and the other lizardmen

04:48.000 --> 04:49.790
to do their laundry and other cleaning.

04:50.750 --> 04:54.830
Well, they do make up for it with how hard
they work to keep the village safe.

04:54.830 --> 04:56.710
I'm glad we have them here.

04:58.330 --> 05:00.170
Hey. Good morning.

05:02.380 --> 05:05.540
Once I've eaten, it's time to
move onto working the fields.

05:06.830 --> 05:08.580
These things again?

05:09.170 --> 05:12.790
None of the normal garden pests
I'm familiar with exist in this world,

05:12.250 --> 05:17.710
<b>Garden Pest (probably)</b>

05:12.790 --> 05:14.830
but instead we have these
weird little black things

05:14.830 --> 05:17.710
that live on the plants and eat their leaves.

05:18.250 --> 05:22.790
Fortunately, Zabuton's kids or Kuro and
the other dogs can spot them for us,

05:22.790 --> 05:25.630
so as of now, they've yet to cause
any real damage.

05:26.000 --> 05:27.710
And the way I deal with them is...

05:29.920 --> 05:33.170
using the almighty farming tool
as a watering can.

05:33.670 --> 05:36.790
Apparently, it has the power to
eliminate garden pests.

05:37.630 --> 05:41.460
The fields that we've been slowly expanding
have become quite large in size.

05:41.460 --> 05:43.420
Checking on all of them is pretty tough now.

05:43.790 --> 05:46.920
But seeing all the matured crops
fills me with joy,

05:46.920 --> 05:49.830
and with a sense of satisfaction
for all the work we've done.

05:51.420 --> 05:54.210
While I'm working on my chores,
lunch time comes around.

05:54.750 --> 05:58.790
I eat the lunch that Anne and the maids
prepared in between my work.

06:01.420 --> 06:05.830
Apparently, having lunch in this world
is very out of the ordinary.

06:06.210 --> 06:08.080
A meal in the afternoon?

06:08.080 --> 06:10.210
But we just ate this morning.

06:10.210 --> 06:13.040
I felt the same way when I first came here.

06:13.500 --> 06:17.630
Lunch aside, Lea and the high elves
were nervous about even eating breakfast.

06:17.630 --> 06:19.750
Is it okay if we eat today, too?

06:19.750 --> 06:22.130
Will our food reserves hold out at this rate?

06:22.130 --> 06:25.710
According to them, they weren't always
able to eat even a single meal each day.

06:25.920 --> 06:28.290
You mean we get to eat food every day?

06:28.290 --> 06:31.880
We're definitely going to get kicked out
of this village, aren't we?!

06:31.880 --> 06:33.790
How did she reach that conclusion?

06:34.330 --> 06:36.330
I want to make sure that none of them

06:36.330 --> 06:38.580
have to worry about food
as long as they're living here.

06:39.540 --> 06:40.540
Mayor.

06:41.290 --> 06:43.420
The cows gave birth to calves.

06:43.420 --> 06:46.040
I'd like to increase their allotted feed.

06:46.040 --> 06:47.630
Yeah, take care of that.

06:47.830 --> 06:51.290
Mayor, our crop storage room
is going to be completely full soon.

06:51.290 --> 06:54.960
Shall we talk to Michael about
selling more of what we produce?

06:54.960 --> 06:57.710
Yeah, let's talk to Flow
and then decide on how much.

07:00.420 --> 07:03.080
After lunch time ends, it's back to work.

07:05.290 --> 07:08.500
Having more people around
has helped with the farmwork a lot.

07:11.380 --> 07:14.750
But tilling new fields or planting new crops
is something I handle myself

07:14.750 --> 07:17.250
with the almighty farming tool.

07:21.170 --> 07:23.710
Up until now, I've only been
growing stuff we could eat,

07:23.710 --> 07:25.420
but I think adding a little color
to our village

07:25.420 --> 07:28.000
is good for making things
feel more civilized.

07:28.540 --> 07:30.500
Outside of the farmwork I do,

07:31.290 --> 07:34.670
the villagers ask me to build
all sorts of little things for them.

07:35.670 --> 07:37.750
Thanks to the almighty farming tool,

07:38.250 --> 07:40.750
I can manage to make things
for them even though I have

07:40.750 --> 07:42.460
no experience in construction.

07:42.790 --> 07:44.750
Once again, I thank God for these blessings.

07:45.420 --> 07:46.500
I also...

07:48.330 --> 07:50.960
like to occasionally join everyone
for their battle training.

07:51.580 --> 07:54.500
I'd like to think we'll never need
this training living here,

07:54.500 --> 07:58.000
but Anne and the maids strongly advised
we hold regular training

07:58.000 --> 08:00.000
just in case anything should happen.

08:00.250 --> 08:03.960
Oh well, getting some more exercise
is good for everyone's health.

08:06.880 --> 08:09.000
Okay, let's keep going!

08:09.000 --> 08:12.830
If we keep eating the way
we do in this village,

08:12.830 --> 08:17.040
one day we'll no longer be able to fit
into our sacred maid uniforms!

08:17.580 --> 08:20.750
I think mine's already starting to
become a tighter fit!

08:20.750 --> 08:21.540
Let's go!

08:21.540 --> 08:23.750
Maybe I need some more exercise...

08:34.790 --> 08:36.670
I'm already at my limit.

08:37.580 --> 08:39.380
I bet I'd be better with that one!

08:39.380 --> 08:40.580
Can I try it out?

08:40.580 --> 08:42.710
Sure, I don't mind.

08:44.670 --> 08:46.210
This is harder than I thought.

08:48.830 --> 08:52.330
I guess I'm really not suited
to use normal weapons.

08:52.330 --> 08:54.290
But I still have this spear!

08:58.130 --> 09:00.790
That was amazing! How did you do that?

09:00.790 --> 09:03.290
I'm not exactly sure when I can use this...

09:04.710 --> 09:06.330
Once the sun starts to set,

09:06.330 --> 09:08.330
I wrap up the work I was doing
and head home.

09:08.630 --> 09:11.080
Oh, I've never seen this dish before.

09:11.080 --> 09:13.540
This is the new menu item
we're trying out today.

09:13.540 --> 09:18.290
It's simmered killer rabbit
served with a sweet honey sauce.

09:18.290 --> 09:19.500
How confident are you?

09:19.500 --> 09:20.880
About 20%.

09:20.880 --> 09:22.250
That's pretty low...

09:22.330 --> 09:23.380
It's sweet!

09:23.380 --> 09:27.210
If possible, I'd like you to only present dishes
that you have at least 50% confidence in...

09:27.210 --> 09:28.630
I cannot do that.

09:28.880 --> 09:31.330
We cannot afford to waste food.

09:31.330 --> 09:32.750
Good point.

09:35.170 --> 09:37.790
I did my best to enjoy the meal.

09:39.290 --> 09:42.460
At dinner time, a lot more people
gather around the table.

09:42.460 --> 09:45.330
We take the chance to report anything
that we want everyone to hear.

09:45.580 --> 09:46.630
Mayor.

09:47.000 --> 09:49.250
Princess Yuri has sent a letter.

09:49.710 --> 09:50.880
Wonder what it is.

09:50.880 --> 09:54.920
Let's see... "I'd like to eat the apples
from your village again.

09:54.920 --> 09:56.830
Also, I'd like a dress."

09:56.830 --> 09:57.880
What is this?

09:57.880 --> 10:01.380
She really liked the clothes
that Zabuton made

10:01.380 --> 10:04.170
and was wondering if she
could have more made for her.

10:04.170 --> 10:05.290
I see.

10:05.290 --> 10:09.540
I apologize. I'll tell her to stop
making so many requests.

10:09.540 --> 10:13.250
Well, I'm sure Zabuton will be
happy to make something for her.

10:15.460 --> 10:19.130
Once I've rested a bit after dinner,
it's bath time.

10:20.750 --> 10:23.420
I pretty much have the men's
bathhouse all to myself.

10:23.790 --> 10:27.040
I couldn't really relax when
we only had one bathhouse.

10:27.040 --> 10:30.540
I'm really glad I forced them
to build a men's bathhouse.

10:32.500 --> 10:34.330
This is paradise.

10:35.500 --> 10:38.000
After I get out of the bath,
it's time to relax...

10:38.000 --> 10:39.920
or at least I wish it was.

10:40.170 --> 10:43.170
This is usually where
I start to feel uneasy.

10:47.500 --> 10:49.170
He's about to enter his house.

10:49.540 --> 10:51.540
I've got eyes on him here.

10:52.210 --> 10:54.330
He's headed straight for his bedroom.

10:54.880 --> 10:55.960
Understood.

10:59.330 --> 11:03.330
Why is it that I can still feel their eyes
on me even though I'm inside my room?

11:05.080 --> 11:07.330
Ah! Someone help me!

11:09.960 --> 11:11.130
Our cover is blown!

11:11.130 --> 11:12.380
Everyone, retreat!
I'm sure they're just keeping watch<b>
</b>because they want to keep me safe.<b></b>

11:12.380 --> 11:15.750
I'm sure they're just keeping watch
because they want to keep me safe.

11:15.750 --> 11:17.420
That's what I tell myself.

11:19.170 --> 11:21.630
Oh well.
Even with stuff like that happening,

11:21.630 --> 11:24.710
I couldn't be happier with
my everyday life here.

11:25.290 --> 11:30.000
God, thank you once again for giving me
a second chance at life here.

11:30.710 --> 11:32.880
I'll do my best again tomorrow.

11:33.750 --> 11:37.710
I need to have those hidden doors
sealed up tomorrow.

11:38.500 --> 11:39.500
Farming Life...

11:39.500 --> 11:40.710
in Another...

11:40.710 --> 11:41.880
World.

11:44.000 --> 11:46.380
Whether it's day or night here in the village,

11:46.380 --> 11:49.540
Donovan and the dwarves are always
hard at work making alcohol.

11:49.880 --> 11:51.960
When it comes to dwarves,

11:49.880 --> 11:51.710
<b>Dwarves</b>

11:49.880 --> 11:51.710
<b>Donovan</b>

11:49.880 --> 11:51.710
<b>Cross</b>

11:49.880 --> 11:51.710
<b>Wilcox</b>

11:51.960 --> 11:55.170
I used to imagine them being merry
and getting drunk all the time.

11:56.000 --> 12:00.330
There's no way we could possibly produce
good alcohol if we were drunk while working!

12:00.330 --> 12:01.750
Indeed, you're right.

12:02.540 --> 12:05.000
Even the man in charge of
watching the fire would...

12:05.000 --> 12:06.830
The man in charge of the fire
drinking on the job?

12:06.830 --> 12:08.000
Out of the question!

12:08.000 --> 12:09.830
That could cause a fire!

12:09.830 --> 12:11.130
Indeed, you're right.

12:11.420 --> 12:14.540
As you can see,
they take their job very seriously.

12:16.710 --> 12:18.670
I think this one came out pretty good.

12:18.670 --> 12:21.210
Nope. This one's no good.

12:21.920 --> 12:23.540
It's lost its flavor and aroma.

12:23.540 --> 12:27.170
This is bad booze that does nothing
but burn your throat.

12:27.170 --> 12:29.540
So, are you going to throw it away?

12:29.540 --> 12:30.750
Nope.

12:30.750 --> 12:32.920
We've still got uses for this.

12:32.920 --> 12:37.080
We'll distill it some more
and then cut it with fruit juice.

12:37.290 --> 12:39.330
Alright, back to the drawing board.

12:39.330 --> 12:41.580
Let's rethink how we're distilling it.

12:41.580 --> 12:45.670
I have nothing but respect for
the passion with which they make alcohol.

12:45.670 --> 12:47.210
Hey, mayor.

12:47.790 --> 12:50.580
Could you increase the amount
of grapes we're harvesting?

12:50.580 --> 12:52.830
I need three times
what we're harvesting now.

12:52.830 --> 12:55.250
Okay... I'll see what I can do.

12:55.670 --> 12:58.790
Increase the harvest. Three times.

12:59.080 --> 13:01.040
Three times, huh?

13:01.040 --> 13:03.540
Well, everyone here really loves their wine.

13:03.540 --> 13:04.830
Mayor!

13:06.040 --> 13:07.250
What is it?

13:08.210 --> 13:10.960
There's this... strange man...

13:11.500 --> 13:13.000
A strange man?

13:18.000 --> 13:19.460
It's a strange man!

13:19.460 --> 13:22.460
How did he even make it this far
in the first place?

13:22.750 --> 13:26.500
He made it by Granmaria
and Zabuton without them noticing?

13:26.710 --> 13:29.040
Oh? Is that the Progenitor?

13:29.210 --> 13:31.210
Lulucy!

13:31.210 --> 13:34.830
Um... the Progenitor?

13:37.130 --> 13:39.330
It's been a long time, Progenitor.

13:39.330 --> 13:41.080
You look like you're doing well, Flora.

13:41.080 --> 13:42.130
I am.

13:42.130 --> 13:44.710
When I first heard that Lulucy was with child,

13:42.250 --> 13:47.580
<b>Progenitor of the Vampires</b>

13:42.250 --> 13:47.580
<b>Vargryfe</b>

13:44.710 --> 13:47.580
I was sure there must have been
some sort of mistake.

13:47.880 --> 13:49.330
It looks like I was wrong.

13:49.330 --> 13:52.130
Yes. I'm quite surprised myself.

13:52.330 --> 13:53.460
That's right.

13:53.460 --> 13:57.540
We vampires usually continue our bloodline
by forming new bloodpacts.

13:57.540 --> 13:58.880
This rarely happens.

13:59.460 --> 14:03.000
But children are a treasure,
and you must take care of yours.

14:03.000 --> 14:05.670
I will. Thank you.

14:06.000 --> 14:07.830
What do you mean he's the Progenitor?

14:08.880 --> 14:13.500
To put it simply, I guess you could say
he's like our grandfather.

14:13.500 --> 14:15.040
Grandfather?

14:15.040 --> 14:16.210
That's right.

14:16.210 --> 14:17.960
I'm about 4,000 years old now.

14:17.960 --> 14:19.250
4,000?

14:19.250 --> 14:21.460
I forget the exact number.

14:21.630 --> 14:25.290
I can't see him as anything other than
a regular young guy.

14:25.290 --> 14:29.290
The trick to leading such a long life
is to occasionally erase your memories.

14:29.290 --> 14:30.420
Your memories?

14:30.420 --> 14:34.580
I make sure to keep the important stuff
like my name and the clan I belong to,

14:34.580 --> 14:37.540
and then I make everything else
go poof and forget about it.

14:37.540 --> 14:40.790
It goes poof? Isn't that kind of scary?

14:40.790 --> 14:44.710
It was scary the first time,
but I got used to it after that.

14:44.710 --> 14:47.580
It's only been about 200 years since
the last time I erased my memories,

14:47.580 --> 14:50.250
so I still feel pretty young now.

14:50.580 --> 14:53.330
I didn't know vampires had that ability.

14:53.330 --> 14:56.250
We don't. I use magic for that.

14:56.250 --> 14:58.540
Magic sounds really useful.

14:58.750 --> 15:03.250
By the way, I'm really sorry that I
entered the village without saying hello.

15:03.250 --> 15:06.330
I'd originally planned to just have
a look around and then quietly leave,

15:06.330 --> 15:08.920
but I was drawn in by a certain presence.

15:08.920 --> 15:09.830
A presence?

15:09.830 --> 15:12.330
That statue below the big tree!

15:12.330 --> 15:14.210
It's wonderful!

15:14.210 --> 15:17.080
It's a splendid likeness of
the great creator!

15:17.080 --> 15:18.960
Before I knew it, I was bowing.

15:18.960 --> 15:20.830
Ah, that's what you meant.

15:21.080 --> 15:23.920
Does that mean you've met God before?

15:23.920 --> 15:26.790
Yes. Just once, when I was born.

15:26.790 --> 15:28.540
He told me to do my best

15:28.540 --> 15:30.460
even though I would be born with
a slightly abnormal body.

15:30.580 --> 15:32.880
And by abnormal body he meant vampire?

15:32.880 --> 15:34.210
I believe so.

15:34.210 --> 15:37.210
Thanks to that, I feel like
I've faced a lot of hardships

15:37.210 --> 15:39.380
and been saved a number of times...

15:39.380 --> 15:42.250
But I can't be sure since
I've erased my memories!

15:42.250 --> 15:45.040
Oh well, I get the feeling
that I've done my best!

15:46.670 --> 15:47.500
Okay.

15:47.830 --> 15:50.920
However, I do remember the creator.

15:51.250 --> 15:54.500
It's just that for some reason,
I can't remember his exact appearance.

15:54.500 --> 15:56.540
Was he an old man?

15:56.540 --> 15:58.250
Or maybe a young man?

15:58.250 --> 16:00.500
What color were his eyes?
What color was his hair?

16:00.500 --> 16:03.630
I've tried numerous times
to create a likeness of him,

16:03.630 --> 16:06.460
but I've never created anything
as accurate as that.

16:07.000 --> 16:09.500
I'm sure living nearby
a masterpiece like that...

16:09.500 --> 16:12.750
means that every single day
of your life is amazing!

16:12.750 --> 16:14.250
It must be so nice!

16:14.250 --> 16:15.960
I'm so jealous!

16:16.630 --> 16:18.000
He wants it, right?

16:18.750 --> 16:21.040
Um, about that statue...

16:21.580 --> 16:25.130
It belongs to the village,
so I don't think I can offer it to you.

16:25.790 --> 16:28.920
I knew it. I get it. But it's too bad...

16:29.380 --> 16:30.790
But it's too bad...

16:30.790 --> 16:33.290
It's too bad, huh?

16:35.790 --> 16:36.130
Too bad...

16:36.130 --> 16:37.380
If you'd like,
Too bad...<b></b>

16:38.040 --> 16:40.040
I could make you a new one.

16:40.040 --> 16:44.210
I'm not a sculptor, so I'm not sure
if you'll like what I make or not.

16:44.210 --> 16:45.290
Really?

16:45.290 --> 16:46.920
I'd love that!

16:46.920 --> 16:49.460
I'm so happy. Thank you!

16:53.000 --> 16:54.670
How do you like it?

16:55.670 --> 16:57.380
I think he likes it.

16:57.380 --> 16:58.670
I think you're right.

16:58.670 --> 17:01.210
Sorry for the sudden request.

17:01.500 --> 17:03.210
How much should I pay you for it?

17:03.210 --> 17:05.710
Nothing. I can't take money for this.

17:06.210 --> 17:09.210
God isn't something
that you're supposed to sell.

17:09.500 --> 17:10.630
I see.

17:11.080 --> 17:14.130
Then I'll have to think about
something else I can do as thanks.

17:14.130 --> 17:14.960
Lu.

17:15.580 --> 17:17.080
Make sure you give birth to a healthy baby.

17:17.080 --> 17:18.170
I will.

17:18.170 --> 17:19.710
Good health to you too, Flora.

17:19.710 --> 17:21.460
And you as well, Progenitor.

17:22.920 --> 17:25.250
Thank you for everything, mayor.

17:25.710 --> 17:27.710
I'm grateful for this statue,

17:27.710 --> 17:29.880
and for what you've done for Lu.

17:29.880 --> 17:31.920
Keep taking care of her, okay?

17:31.920 --> 17:32.920
I will.

17:36.500 --> 17:39.880
I was a little surprised at first,
but he seems like an easygoing guy.

17:39.880 --> 17:40.960
He sure is.

17:40.960 --> 17:44.250
And to think, he's such an incredibly
important and high-ranking person.

17:45.880 --> 17:47.920
Is he really that important?

17:48.540 --> 17:50.630
My lord!

17:50.880 --> 17:52.920
Welcome back.

17:52.920 --> 17:55.380
It's been a while.
How many years does this make?

17:55.380 --> 17:58.170
I believe it's been 50 years now.

17:58.170 --> 18:01.630
As you can see, I've become an old man.

18:02.330 --> 18:04.380
So you're in charge of the temple now?

18:04.380 --> 18:07.040
Yes, for about 30 years now.

18:07.040 --> 18:09.580
Well you've always been a devout believer.

18:09.580 --> 18:11.250
You're the man for the job.

18:11.250 --> 18:13.130
Thank you very much.

18:13.580 --> 18:14.920
Has anything changed?

18:14.920 --> 18:18.830
Not a thing. Everything is as it always was.

18:18.830 --> 18:19.880
I see.

18:19.880 --> 18:21.750
I'm glad to hear that,

18:21.750 --> 18:23.960
but there's going to be
a big change starting today.

18:23.960 --> 18:25.920
What might you mean by that?

18:25.920 --> 18:28.630
I want to enshrine this statue
here in this temple.

18:28.630 --> 18:31.250
You do? What kind of statue is that?

18:31.250 --> 18:33.040
You'll just have to wait and see.

18:33.040 --> 18:35.170
I want you to put it in the best spot here.

18:35.420 --> 18:37.670
Well, that would mean...

18:37.670 --> 18:41.080
We'd have to move
the statue of the creator

18:41.080 --> 18:43.460
that was crafted by the
master sculptor, Toorook.

18:43.460 --> 18:46.830
I don't know if we can simply move
the most beloved statue in this temple

18:46.830 --> 18:48.210
from its resting place...

18:48.210 --> 18:50.170
Yeah. Sure we can.

18:50.420 --> 18:51.540
Yes, sir.

18:55.330 --> 18:59.670
This is such... a majestic work of art.

18:59.670 --> 19:02.750
It must have been made by
quite a famous sculptor.

19:02.750 --> 19:06.080
We must be sure that everyone
properly honors their name.

19:06.080 --> 19:07.960
I think it would be better if we didn't.

19:08.540 --> 19:12.290
He doesn't seem like the type
to appreciate stuff like that.

19:12.670 --> 19:16.040
Besides, I don't want to do anything
to disturb his peaceful life.

19:16.670 --> 19:18.460
That is most unfortunate.

19:18.750 --> 19:22.210
But I don't think it would be a problem
if we were to quietly support him.

19:22.210 --> 19:23.330
Indeed.

19:23.330 --> 19:25.830
Let all the other temples know immediately.

19:25.830 --> 19:28.920
Tell them to be respectful of him,

19:28.920 --> 19:30.960
as well as respectful of
The Great Tree Village.

19:30.960 --> 19:32.040
Right away.

19:33.670 --> 19:35.130
Are you okay?

19:35.130 --> 19:36.670
Y-yeah.

19:36.670 --> 19:38.710
That caught me off guard.

19:38.710 --> 19:41.210
It's been a long time since I've sneezed.

19:44.250 --> 19:47.460
The Progenitor sent us a magnificent piano.

19:48.210 --> 19:50.420
I refused to take payment for the statue,

19:50.420 --> 19:52.750
so he said this was a gift
to celebrate Lu's pregnancy.

19:52.750 --> 19:54.960
He's really considerate
for someone so important.

19:56.880 --> 19:59.170
We talked for a while
about where we would put it.

19:59.170 --> 20:01.080
There we go.

20:01.540 --> 20:03.880
We decided to place it
in the village's dining hall.

20:03.880 --> 20:05.750
Thanks guys. Good work.

20:05.750 --> 20:07.170
Good work, everyone.

20:07.670 --> 20:09.330
That piano...

20:09.330 --> 20:12.580
Is it the kind that you would
only find in a large temple?

20:12.580 --> 20:16.460
Yeah. That's the kind of piano
that only gets used for big ceremonies.

20:16.460 --> 20:18.830
Hey, hey.
Do you think it's okay if we play it?

20:18.830 --> 20:20.920
Yeah, this is a once in a lifetime-

20:20.920 --> 20:24.330
No... it's more like a
never in a lifetime chance.

20:25.380 --> 20:28.000
That means if we can play this piano now,

20:28.000 --> 20:30.750
we'll be able to brag about this
for the rest of our lives!

20:34.830 --> 20:36.290
You can go first.

20:37.420 --> 20:39.170
I'm fine with playing later, too.

20:43.250 --> 20:46.420
This thing is way too scary
for us to even try playing!

20:46.420 --> 20:48.500
My hands are sweating so much!

20:48.500 --> 20:51.380
If we break it,
that'll be the end of our lives!

20:52.500 --> 20:54.330
You want another piano?

20:54.330 --> 20:56.250
F-for us to practice on.

20:56.250 --> 20:59.880
Please. We don't mind
if it's old and beat up.

20:59.880 --> 21:02.380
Actually, an old piano would be best.

21:02.750 --> 21:04.540
Can't you play the one we already have?

21:04.540 --> 21:06.670
No, we can't!

21:06.670 --> 21:09.080
Huh? You're crying?

21:09.880 --> 21:14.130
We talked to Michael and had him
procure a practice piano for us.

21:18.000 --> 21:20.210
I don't really know anything about these,

21:20.210 --> 21:23.130
but the one we got from
the Progenitor seems a lot fancier.

21:23.130 --> 21:26.540
Now I feel bad that he sent us
something so nice.

21:30.960 --> 21:33.670
The pianos were hit.
Everyone wanted to play.

21:35.580 --> 21:37.210
The only ones who could already play well

21:37.210 --> 21:39.790
were Flowrem and the girls from
the Demonic Kingdom,

21:41.130 --> 21:44.670
but everyone else seems to enjoy
practicing to get better.

22:11.580 --> 22:13.790
I just wish they'd stop playing at night...

22:30.210 --> 22:38.960
I can feel the soft seasonal winds,
gently on my fingertips

22:39.290 --> 22:47.880
Let's search for what we love
in the clouds floating in the sky

22:47.880 --> 22:52.670
Forget about the hands of the clock for now

22:52.670 --> 22:57.080
Try taking one deep breath

22:57.080 --> 23:06.710
The rainbow-colored scenery
will resonate with my heart

23:08.040 --> 23:13.040
I'm sure any wish I have will come true

23:13.040 --> 23:17.580
Because you're by my side

23:17.580 --> 23:22.170
You make every day feel like a dream

23:22.420 --> 23:26.960
At that warm and kind place

23:26.960 --> 23:34.130
Keep showing me your smiling face forever

23:46.040 --> 23:47.380
<b>Next Time</b>

23:47.380 --> 23:50.960
<b>Episode 12</b>

23:47.380 --> 23:50.960
<b>Birth</b>

23:47.380 --> 23:50.960
<b>Next Time</b>
